<%- include('partials/top', { title: 'Settings' }) %>
<section class="to-section-head"><h1>Settings</h1></section>
<section class="to-panel">
  <h2>Escalation and the complaint nudge</h2>
  <% if (alertsReady) { %><p>A reply with nobody approving it within the first time goes red on Today, and a manager is emailed once. A complaint with no approved reply within the second time is passed up to a manager, who is emailed once. Nothing is ever sent to the customer automatically.</p>
  <% } else { %><p>A reply with nobody approving it within the first time goes red on Today. A complaint with no approved reply within the second time is passed up to a manager and shows on Today. Alert emails are not set up yet, so nobody is emailed: Today is the only warning. Nothing is ever sent to the customer automatically.</p><% } %>
  <% if (atLeast(user, 'owner')) { %>
  <form method="post" action="/settings" class="to-form">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
    <div class="to-field-row">
      <label class="to-field"><span>Hours before any reply is overdue</span><input name="escalation_hours" type="number" min="1" max="168" value="<%= hours %>" required></label>
      <label class="to-field"><span>Hours before a complaint goes to a manager</span><input name="complaint_nudge_hours" type="number" min="1" max="168" value="<%= nudgeHours %>" required></label>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="to-btn to-btn-primary">Save</button>
  </form>
  <% } else { %><p class="to-status-line">Currently <strong><%= hours %> hours</strong> for any reply and <strong><%= nudgeHours %> hours</strong> for a complaint. The owner changes these.</p><% } %>
</section>
<section class="to-panel" id="prices">
  <h2>Fixed prices</h2>
  <p>Airports and the like. The AI quotes a price only when a customer's journey matches a line here, in either direction. For every other journey it gives no price and says the office will confirm it.</p>
  <% if (prices.length) { %>
  <div class="to-table-wrap"><table class="to-table to-prices">
    <thead><tr><% if (manyBrands) { %><th scope="col">Brand</th><% } %><th scope="col">From</th><th scope="col">To</th><th scope="col">Vehicle</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">Notes</th><th scope="col"></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody><% prices.forEach(function (p) { %>
      <tr><% if (manyBrands) { %><td><%= brandName(p.brand) %></td><% } %><td><%= p.from_place %></td><td><%= p.to_place %></td><td><%= p.vehicle %></td><td class="to-num">£<%= (p.price_pence / 100).toFixed(2) %></td><td><%= p.notes %></td>
        <td><form method="post" action="/settings/prices/<%= p.id %>/delete"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><button type="submit" class="to-btn to-btn-quiet" data-confirm="Remove this price?">Remove</button></form></td></tr>
    <% }) %></tbody>
  </table></div>
  <% } else { %><p class="to-empty">No fixed prices yet, so the AI quotes nothing. Add the airport runs and any other set fares below.</p><% } %>
  <form method="post" action="/settings/prices" class="to-form">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
    <div class="to-field-row">
      <label class="to-field"><span>From</span><input name="from_place" maxlength="120" required placeholder="Falmouth"></label>
      <label class="to-field"><span>To</span><input name="to_place" maxlength="120" required placeholder="Newquay Airport"></label>
    </div>
    <div class="to-field-row">
      <label class="to-field"><span>Vehicle</span><select name="vehicle"><% ['Car (up to 4)', 'Estate (up to 4, more luggage)', '6 seater', '8 seater', 'Wheelchair accessible'].forEach(function (v) { %><option><%= v %></option><% }) %></select></label>
      <label class="to-field"><span>Price in pounds</span><input name="price" inputmode="decimal" required placeholder="65 or 65.50"></label>
    </div>
    <div class="to-field-row">
      <label class="to-field"><span>Notes (optional)</span><input name="notes" maxlength="200" placeholder="Daytime, up to 2 cases each"></label>
      <% if (manyBrands && !user.brand) { %><label class="to-field"><span>Brand</span><select name="brand"><% brands.forEach(function (b) { %><option value="<%= b.id %>"><%= b.name %></option><% }) %></select></label><% } %>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="to-btn to-btn-primary">Add price</button>
  </form>
</section>
<section class="to-panel" id="mailbox">
  <h2>The bookings mailbox</h2>
  <% if (mailboxDemo) { %>
  <p>The office is reading a made-up inbox. The firm's real mailbox is connected only once the data processing agreement between the firm and Arrington Consultancy is signed.</p>
  <% } else if (mailboxNone) { %>
  <p>No mailbox is connected, and it stays that way until the data processing agreement between the firm and Arrington Consultancy is signed. Nothing is read from, or saved to, any mailbox. Approved replies are copied out by hand.</p>
  <% } else if (mailConnect.stored.connected) { %>
  <p class="to-status-line"><strong><%= mailConnect.stored.account %></strong> is connected<% if (mailConnect.stored.by) { %>, by <%= mailConnect.stored.by %><% } %><% if (mailConnect.stored.at) { %> on <%= new Date(mailConnect.stored.at).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'Europe/London' }) %><% } %>. The office reads its inbox and saves approved replies there as drafts. It never sends.</p>
  <% } else if (mailConnect.envToken) { %>
  <p class="to-status-line">Connected through a token set on the server for <strong><%= mailConnect.address %></strong>. It reads the inbox and saves drafts. It never sends.</p>
  <% } else { %>
  <p>Not connected yet. Whoever can sign in to <strong><%= mailConnect.address || 'the bookings mailbox' %></strong> presses Connect, signs in to Google as that mailbox and presses Allow. The office checks Google gives back that exact address and refuses any other.</p>
  <% } %>
  <% if (!mailboxDemo && !mailboxNone && atLeast(user, 'owner')) { %>
    <% if (mailConnect.keyReady && !mailConnect.clientInRailway) { %>
    <form method="post" action="/settings/mailbox/client" class="to-form" autocomplete="off">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
      <p class="to-small"><%= mailConnect.stored.clientFromSettings ? 'Google client saved' + (mailConnect.stored.clientId ? ' (' + mailConnect.stored.clientId.slice(0, 12) + '...)' : '') + '. Enter it again only to replace it.' : 'First, the Google client details from the firm\'s Google Cloud project (see the steps below). They are typed in here so the secret never travels by email or chat.' %></p>
      <div class="to-field-row">
        <label class="to-field"><span>Client ID</span><input id="client_id" name="client_id" maxlength="120" required spellcheck="false" placeholder="ends .apps.googleusercontent.com"></label>
        <label class="to-field"><span>Client secret</span><input id="client_secret" name="client_secret" type="password" maxlength="80" required spellcheck="false"></label>
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="to-btn">Save the client details</button>
    </form>
    <% } %>
    <% if (mailConnect.ready) { %>
    <div class="to-actions">
      <a class="to-btn <%= mailConnect.stored.connected ? '' : 'to-btn-primary' %>" href="/settings/mailbox/connect"><%= mailConnect.stored.connected ? 'Connect again' : 'Connect the mailbox' %></a>
      <% if (mailConnect.stored.connected) { %>
      <form method="post" action="/settings/mailbox/disconnect" class="to-inline-form"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><button type="submit" class="to-btn to-btn-quiet" data-confirm="Disconnect the mailbox? The office stops reading it straight away and the token is cancelled at Google.">Disconnect</button></form>
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <p class="to-small">Google asks to read the mailbox and to create drafts in it. The office reads the inbox and saves replies as drafts only; a person sends them from the mailbox.</p>
    <% } else { %>
    <p class="to-small">Before it can be connected, this is still needed: <%= mailConnect.blockers.join('; ') %>.</p>
    <% } %>
  <% } %>
  <% if (!mailboxNone) { %>
  <details class="to-details">
    <summary>Setting up the Google side (for whoever runs the firm's Google account)</summary>
    <ol class="to-steps">
      <li>In Google Cloud, in the firm's own Google Workspace, create a project and enable the Gmail API.</li>
      <li>OAuth consent screen: user type Internal, so only the firm's own accounts can use it. Internal needs no Google review, and its tokens do not expire after seven days.</li>
      <li>Credentials, Create OAuth client ID, Web application. Authorised redirect URI, exactly: <code><%= baseUrl %><%= mailConnect.redirectUri %></code></li>
      <li>Sign in here as the owner and type the client ID and secret into the form above. Never send them by email or message.</li>
      <li>Press Connect the mailbox and sign in to Google as the bookings mailbox.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="to-small">If the mailbox is a free Gmail account rather than Google Workspace, Internal is not available. Use an app password over IMAP instead; Arrington sets that up.</p>
  </details>
  <% } %>
</section>
<section class="to-panel">
  <h2>Connections</h2>
  <p class="to-small">Set on the server by Arrington, never from this page. Values are never shown here.</p>
  <ul class="to-history">
    <li><time>Mailbox</time><span><%= mailStatus.replace(/^Abacus office mailbox: /, '') %></span></li>
    <li><time>Dispatch</time><span><%= dispatchStatus.replace(/^Abacus office dispatch: /, '') %><% if (dispatchLive) { %> <a href="/settings/icabbi-vehicles">See iCabbi's vehicle types</a><% } %></span></li>
    <li><time>AI</time><span><%= aiStatus.replace(/^Abacus office AI: /, '') %></span></li>
    <li><time>Alerts</time><span><%= alertStatus.replace(/^Abacus office alerts: /, '') %></span></li>
  </ul>
</section>
<%- include('partials/bottom') %>
